WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.830
The human beta-globin gene is transcribed
into a first RNA copy 1608 bases long.

2
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.140
Yet most of that copy
never reaches the ribosome.

3
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.840
It is cut and changed inside the nucleus,

4
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.310
before the finished message leaves.

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:20.050
So what is kept, and why
does that choice matter?

6
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.020
In this mission, you'll
follow one first copy,

7
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.100
a pre-mRNA, as it becomes
a finished message.

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.880
Then you'll measure every section of the
real beta-globin gene and work out how

9
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.430
much is cut.

10
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.260
Your mission: find out what is
kept from a gene's first RNA copy,

11
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.550
and why it matters.
